{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfu1n5ZuysJZSCLdmrkxC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Build it, with a randomized holdout from day one. Don't do a separate research phase first.**\n\n**Why build**\n- The email result is strong evidence. It was randomized, and late collection fell from 31% to 18%. With about 400 patients per arm, the 95% interval on that 13-point drop is roughly 7 to 19 points. Even the low end is worth having.\n- The no-reminder arm (31%) matches your pharmacy-wide rate. That suggests email opt-in patients aren't unusually prompt, which makes the result more believable.\n- Reminders are cheap, and three weeks of two engineers is a small bet. More research up front would delay a likely win without changing the decision.\n\n**What the evidence doesn't tell you**\n- Push is a different channel. Opt-in rates, delivery, and attention differ, so don't assume 13 points.\n- Push users may differ from email-opt-in users.\n- The trial measured collection timing, not adherence or health outcomes.\n\n**How to build it so it answers those questions**\n1. Ship push to the app's opted-in users, but keep a random holdout of about 10–20% with no reminder. Keep it running, so you measure the effect rather than assume it.\n2. Reuse the email reminder's timing and wording, since that's what was tested. Change one thing at a time later.\n3. Keep the notification text generic. Don't show medication names on a lock screen.\n4. Track push permission rate, opens, and late collection (more than 7 days) against the holdout.\n5. Set a decision rule up front, such as \"keep if late collection drops by at least 5 points.\"\n\n**Research worth doing in parallel (cheap):** check whether push-permission rates are high enough to matter. If few patients would receive it, the impact shrinks and email expansion may be the better use of the time."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3204,"cache_read_input_tokens":5027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3204},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f43c15a7-0dfc-42d3-8cec-c514e5fd5df1","uuid":"fd7571d0-da83-4b0b-83ef-9079434db740","timestamp":"2026-10-10T18:16:40.664Z","request_id":"req_011Cfu1n5KnBMZwMUYPnGiG2"}
